      "path": "src/ui/screens/ReviewReflections.tsx",
      "content": "This treats both non-due classifications as due in the next Review. A Close Review for a position change after the current session close is classified as `DueInReviewAfterNext`, so this message contradicts the group's due-status heading and tells the trader it is due one Review too early. Distinguish `DueInNextReview` from `DueInReviewAfterNext` (or reuse `DUE_TEXT[reflection.classification]`).",
      "existing_code": "      {!resolved \u0026\u0026 !isOpen \u0026\u0026 closeReview \u0026\u0026 reflection.classification !== 'Due' \u0026\u0026 \u003cp\u003eNot due until the next Review.\u003c/p\u003e}",
      "start_line": 81,
      "end_line": 81,
      "category": "bug",
      "severity": "medium"
    },
    {
      "path": "src/ui/screens/ReviewOwedCard.tsx",
      "content": "A due Position Change Reflection takes precedence over these Close Review states because the `dueNow \u003e 0` return runs first. Consequently, a closed card whose Close Review is next-review, saved, or declined is labelled only “1 reflection due”, contrary to the Close Review-based labelling requirement. Resolve all available Close Review states before falling back to the generic reflection count, and add cases with a due-now Position Change Reflection (the current status tests use only a not-yet-due one).",
      "existing_code": "  if (closeReview?.classification === 'DueInNextReview') return 'Close Review · next Review';\n  const outcome = typeof detail === 'object' \u0026\u0026 detail.card.summary?.kind === 'Closed' ? detail.card.summary.closeReviewOutcome?.kind : undefined;\n  if (!closeReview \u0026\u0026 outcome === 'Entry') return 'Close Review saved';\n  if (!closeReview \u0026\u0026 outcome === 'Decline') return 'Close Review declined';",
